<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>FADE IN:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="1"><Text>INT. ARJUN'S HOUSE - KITCHEN - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A narrow Mumbai kitchen. Steel utensils gleam on open shelves. Rain hammers the window grille.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>DADI (80s), wrapped in a white cotton saree, sits on a low stool by the window shelling peas into a steel bowl. She does not look up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ARJUN (45), shirt half-buttoned, gulps chai standing up. MEERA (40) packs a tiffin with brisk, practised movements.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You didn't sleep again.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>The accounts don't balance. Forty lakhs, Meera. Gone.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(lowering her voice)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Is it Vikram?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Don't say his name in this house.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dadi's hands pause over the bowl. Then continue.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KABIR (O.S.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Papa! I'm going to be late!</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun grabs the tiffin, kisses Meera's forehead, and hurries out.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="2"><Text>EXT. ARJUN'S HOUSE - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A crumbling chawl courtyard flooded ankle-deep. KABIR (10), school bag over his head, waits under a dripping tin awning.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Across the courtyard, MRS. D'SOUZA (60s) waves from her balcony. Arjun waves back without breaking stride.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KABIR</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Can we take the car today? Please?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Not today, beta. Today we walk.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They wade out through the gate, Kabir holding his father's sleeve.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="3"><Text>INT. CITY HOSPITAL - ICU - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Monitors beep in a dim, crowded ward. Every bed is taken.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>DR. RAO (50s), tired eyes behind steel-rimmed glasses, studies a chart. NURSE LATA (30s) adjusts an IV drip.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera stands at the foot of a bed, clutching her dupatta, silent.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DR. RAO</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>The surgery has to happen this week. After that, I can promise nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>NURSE LATA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>The deposit has to be paid first, Doctor. Accounts won't release the theatre.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DR. RAO</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(to Meera, gently)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Has your husband arranged the money?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera can't answer. Dr. Rao exchanges a look with Lata.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>NURSE LATA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Tell Arjun-ji to come to the billing counter tomorrow.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="4"><Text>INT. CITY HOSPITAL - CORRIDOR - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long corridor lit by flickering tube lights. Families sleep on newspapers along the walls.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun, soaked through, finds Meera sitting on a bench.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>How much?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Six lakhs. By Friday.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dr. Rao walks past them, files under his arm. He nods at Arjun but doesn't stop.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I'll get it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>From where? From him?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun doesn't answer. He sits beside her and takes her hand.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="5"><Text>EXT. CRAWFORD MARKET - DUSK</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A huge crowd of shoppers jostles between fruit stalls under blue tarpaulins. Hawkers shout prices. Rain has eased to a drizzle.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>THREE GOONS in matching black shirts shove through the crowd, clearing a path.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Behind them strolls VIKRAM (50), white kurta, gold chain, an umbrella held over him by one of the goons.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun waits by a mango stall. He straightens as Vikram arrives.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>GOON 1</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Bhai is busy. Make it quick.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Arjun. My old friend. You look terrible.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I need six lakhs. I'll pay it back with interest.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(smiling)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You still owe me from last time. And the time before that.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Vikram picks up a mango, smells it, puts it back.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>VIKRAM (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Bring me the ledger. Then we'll talk about money.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He walks away. The goons follow. The crowd closes behind them.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="6"><Text>INT./EXT. ARJUN'S CAR - MOVING - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>An old Maruti crawls through flooded traffic. Wipers struggle against the rain.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun drives, phone wedged against his shoulder.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He wants the ledger.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(over phone)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Then give it to him. Kabir needs his mother more than you need your pride.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>If I give it to him, he owns us forever.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He already does.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The line goes dead. Arjun stares at the phone, then at the road.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="7"><Text>INT. ARJUNS HOUSE - BEDROOM - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dark except for a bedside lamp. Arjun sits on the edge of the bed holding an old framed photograph: two boys on a riverbank, arms around each other's shoulders. Vikram and Arjun, decades ago.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He turns the frame over. Taped to the back is a small brass key.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He peels the key off and closes his fist around it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>DISSOLVE TO:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="8"><Text>EXT. VILLAGE RIVERBANK - DAY (FLASHBACK)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Bright sun on a wide brown river. Buffaloes wallow in the shallows.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>YOUNG ARJUN (10) and YOUNG VIKRAM (12) sit on a rock, feet in the water, sharing a stolen guava.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>YOUNG VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>When we're big, we'll run the whole city. You keep the accounts. I'll keep the people in line.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>YOUNG ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And we'll never lie to each other.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>YOUNG VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Never.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They spit in their palms and shake.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="8A"><Text>EXT. VILLAGE RIVERBANK - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The sun is lower. Young Arjun sits alone on the rock, scratching numbers into the stone with a pebble, adding and re-adding a column that will not balance.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="9"><Text>OMITTED</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. POLICE STATION - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A cramped station house. Files tied with red string are stacked to the ceiling. A ceiling fan turns lazily.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>INSPECTOR SHARMA (40s), crisp khaki, reads a newspaper with his boots on the desk. A CONSTABLE stands at the door, watching the rain.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun sits across from Sharma, the brass key on the desk between them.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INSPECTOR SHARMA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A key. You came in this weather to show me a key.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It opens a locker at the cooperative bank. Inside is a ledger. Every payment Vikram ever made to anyone in this city.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Sharma folds the newspaper slowly.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SHARMA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Including to people in this building?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Including to you.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The Constable glances over his shoulder, then quickly looks away.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SHARMA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quietly)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Go home, Arjun. Before you get hurt.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="11"><Text>EXT. CITY HOSPITAL - DAWN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>First grey light over the hospital gate. Rain has finally stopped. Street dogs sleep under parked ambulances.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera and Kabir sit on the hospital steps sharing a packet of glucose biscuits. Nurse Lata comes out, pulls off her mask, and sits two steps above them without a word.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KABIR</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Is Papa coming?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He promised.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kabir leans against her shoulder.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="12"><Text>HOSPITAL ROOFTOP - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Water tanks and satellite dishes. The city glitters below, wet and endless.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun stands near the edge holding a plastic-wrapped ledger. Vikram steps out of the stairwell door. Behind him, several of his men take up positions in the shadows.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You went to the police. That was stupid, even for you.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You said never lie to each other. Remember?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>We were children.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I wasn't.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun holds the ledger out over the edge. Vikram's men step forward. Vikram raises a hand and they stop.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>VIKRAM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What do you want?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>The hospital bill. Paid in full. And you never come near my family again.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long beat. Vikram nods.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="13"><Text>INT. ARJUN'S HOUSE - KITCHEN - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The same kitchen, now quiet. The window is open; the rain has gone.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera washes cups at the sink. Kabir sleeps with his head on the table. Dadi is back on her stool by the window.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The door opens. Arjun enters, exhausted, empty-handed.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Is it over?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun looks at Dadi. For the first time, the old woman looks up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DADI</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nothing is ever over, beta. Sit. Eat.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun sits. Meera puts a plate in front of him.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="14"><Text>EXT. ARJUN'S HOUSE - TERRACE - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun and Meera sit on the terrace parapet. Lines of washing flap in the breeze. Far away, thunder.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Will he keep his word?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>For a while.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And after that?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>After that, I keep the accounts.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She leans her head on his shoulder. The first drops of new rain begin to fall.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>FADE OUT.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>THE END</Text></Paragraph>
</Content><TitlePage><Content>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>MONSOON LEDGER</Text></Paragraph>
